Anthony, 2026-10-25: "Go with a + b, then c". This is option b of fact:root-cause-a-fix-rarely-records-what-it-answered-because-it-is-a-separate-call-2026-10-25, done after `answers` (dec:a-fix-names-the-findings-it-answers-in-the-same-call) is built. The pass works in three batches:
- the 100 findings a fixing commit, CHANGELOG entry or change record names: each is checked against the code at main, then closed with INVALIDATES from the change that answered it (or, if it is still open, kept with a note saying so);
- the 64 backlog rows imported at 2026-08-07: walked the same way;
- the 216 named nowhere: in batches, each checked against today's code and behaviour.
Every finding ends as fixed (INVALIDATES from the answering change), still open (kept, and ranked for work), or obsolete (valid_to, with the reason). The check for each one is a measurement, never a guess. Nothing is deleted. Done one batch per design-writing PR, under the design hold. After it, choices_in_doubt and the open-breach line show news rather than backlog.
